AV1: treat full-refresh Delayed Random Access Points as keyframes

A Temporal Unit that carries a Sequence Header and opens with a hidden Key
Frame (show_frame = 0) refreshing all eight reference slots can be decoded
from directly, since nothing before it is reachable afterwards. Upstream
treats it as an inter frame twice over: av1_parser sets key_frame only for
a shown Key Frame, and for Matroska video (opened with
AVSTREAM_PARSE_HEADERS) that verdict replaces the block's own flag; and
muxers (mkvmerge, lavf) leave the SimpleBlock flag off, so matroskadec
never builds an index and every seek fails. An encode built on such
forward key frames then reaches the caller without a single keyframe
(AetherEngine issue 931).

ff_av1_is_random_access_point() (libavformat/av1.c) reads the first frame
header up to refresh_frame_flags; matroskadec flags an unflagged, unlaced,
unencoded AV1 SimpleBlock that passes it, and av1_parser reports the same
case as a key frame. A hidden Key Frame with a partial refresh, which
libaom writes for --enable-fwd-kf, is left alone: frames after it still
reference the previous shown Key Frame.

Three commits upstream as FFmpeg PR 25607, squashed here against n8.1.3.

